{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463508",
      "title": "Emitting Custom Events (Child => Parent Communication)",
      "lectureOrder": 99,
      "videoOrder": 84,
      "sourceHash": "770bb27ad04fd511c6f84684bd636dbafe56c9580812392551713f30a1a162b2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.11,
          "end": 5.06,
          "en": "So that's it for props for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.06,
          "end": 8.397,
          "en": "We're using props to pass data from the app.vue file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.397,
          "end": 11.4,
          "en": "into our FriendContact component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.4,
          "end": 14.253,
          "en": "Now what about communication from the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.253,
          "end": 15.88,
          "en": "to the parent?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.88,
          "end": 18.57,
          "en": "A good example would be toggle favorite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.57,
          "end": 21.862,
          "en": "At the moment, this is kind of a dummy thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.862,
          "end": 25.89,
          "en": "I'm setting it to true for every generated friend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.89,
          "end": 29.7,
          "en": "And we're not really managing it on a friend specific level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.7,
          "end": 32.891,
          "en": "Yes, I can toggle it for an individual friend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.891,
          "end": 36.03,
          "en": "but that only changes inside of the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.03,
          "end": 39.027,
          "en": "In reality, just like the name, the phone number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.027,
          "end": 40.91,
          "en": "the email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.91,
          "end": 44.67,
          "en": "is-favorite should not be set to true like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.67,
          "end": 47.93,
          "en": "Instead, we should probably have a isFavorite property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.93,
          "end": 52.066,
          "en": "on our friend object so that this data is really stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.066,
          "end": 54.93,
          "en": "on the input data, where we have the rest",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.93,
          "end": 56.763,
          "en": "of our friends data as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.89,
          "end": 61.733,
          "en": "So we could have isFavorite here and also here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.77,
          "end": 66.11,
          "en": "That's what we typically would want to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.11,
          "end": 67.31,
          "en": "because the information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.31,
          "end": 69.667,
          "en": "whether a friend is a favorite of us or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.667,
          "end": 73.22,
          "en": "is just as important and friend specific",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.22,
          "end": 76.76,
          "en": "as its phone number and email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.76,
          "end": 79.3,
          "en": "And it's not just something which we want to change here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.3,
          "end": 80.7,
          "en": "inside of a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.7,
          "end": 83.69,
          "en": "It should be part of our core friends data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.69,
          "end": 87.61,
          "en": "which could be coming from a database or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.61,
          "end": 90.2,
          "en": "Now we got isFavorite managed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.2,
          "end": 93.30799999999999,
          "en": "and of course we can pass that down to our component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.30799999999999,
          "end": 98.283,
          "en": "but there, again, it just acts as an initial prop value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.283,
          "end": 101.44,
          "en": "which means if I click toggle favorite here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.44,
          "end": 104.97,
          "en": "that changes it inside of the FriendContact component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.97,
          "end": 108.083,
          "en": "but not inside of our core friends data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.21000000000001,
          "end": 111.449,
          "en": "Here of course, that is just some dummy data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.449,
          "end": 114.1,
          "en": "but if this would be coming from a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.1,
          "end": 116.59,
          "en": "we probably would want to send it back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.59,
          "end": 118.52000000000001,
          "en": "to that database as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.52000000000001,
          "end": 122.62,
          "en": "So just changing it inside of that component is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.62,
          "end": 126.095,
          "en": "We would also want to change it here in app.vue file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.095,
          "end": 129.233,
          "en": "in our friends data, in our friends array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.25,
          "end": 132.97,
          "en": "So therefore, we now need communication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.97,
          "end": 136.89,
          "en": "from the FriendContact component back to app.vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.89,
          "end": 139.542,
          "en": "So basically the opposite of props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.542,
          "end": 143.03,
          "en": "Props allowed us to pass data from app.vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.03,
          "end": 144.86,
          "en": "to FriendContact.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.86,
          "end": 149.49,
          "en": "Now we need a way of letting FriendContact tell app.vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.49,
          "end": 152.04,
          "en": "that the favorite status changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.04,
          "end": 155.34,
          "en": "and how could that work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.34,
          "end": 157.013,
          "en": "How could we implement that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.45,
          "end": 163.12,
          "en": "Well, how does it work for regular HTML elements?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.12,
          "end": 164.81,
          "en": "If we click a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.81,
          "end": 167.6,
          "en": "the button in the end wants to let us know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.6,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "that it was clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "So the button emits a click event to which we can listen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 177.18,
          "en": "And it's the same for custom components in Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.18,
          "end": 181.284,
          "en": "If a component should talk to its parent and let the parent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.284,
          "end": 183.209,
          "en": "know that something happened,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.209,
          "end": 185.878,
          "en": "that component should emit an event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.878,
          "end": 188.78,
          "en": "to which the parent can listen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.78,
          "end": 192.262,
          "en": "And indeed you can emit your own custom events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.262,
          "end": 195.06,
          "en": "inside of your Vue components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.06,
          "end": 199.275,
          "en": "For example here, when toggleFavorite is triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.275,
          "end": 202.032,
          "en": "In this method, instead of changing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.032,
          "end": 206.797,
          "en": "this internal friendIsFavorite data property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.797,
          "end": 211.15,
          "en": "we can use this and now a built in method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.15,
          "end": 213.57999999999998,
          "en": "which ships together with Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.57999999999998,
          "end": 216.24,
          "en": "and therefore it starts with a dollar sign,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.24,
          "end": 219.808,
          "en": "just like refs did in the behind the scenes module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.808,
          "end": 223.683,
          "en": "But now it's not refs, but emit, dollar sign emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.69,
          "end": 229.28,
          "en": "That's a built in method, which you can call from inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.28,
          "end": 232.98,
          "en": "a Vue component under this keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.98,
          "end": 236.91,
          "en": "And this allows you to emit your own custom event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.91,
          "end": 238.57999999999998,
          "en": "to which you then can listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.57999999999998,
          "end": 240.763,
          "en": "from inside the parent component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.34,
          "end": 245.49,
          "en": "Now emit wants at least one argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.49,
          "end": 249.13,
          "en": "and that is the name of the custom event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 249.13,
          "end": 251.78,
          "en": "And here you can name this event, however you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.78,
          "end": 252.62,
          "en": "It's your event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252.62,
          "end": 254.27,
          "en": "So you can use any name you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 255.4,
          "end": 257.84,
          "en": "And I'll use toggle-favorite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 257.84,
          "end": 260.791,
          "en": "Here the convention is to always use kebab case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.791,
          "end": 262.993,
          "en": "no matter where you use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 263.963,
          "end": 267.19,
          "en": "So that's different to props where in the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 267.19,
          "end": 270.031,
          "en": "that receives it, you use camel case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 270.031,
          "end": 274.40999999999997,
          "en": "and you only use kebab case for passing in the values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.40999999999997,
          "end": 277.7,
          "en": "For events it's always kebab case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 277.7,
          "end": 280.76,
          "en": "So now we're emitting this toggle favorite event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.76,
          "end": 284.133,
          "en": "Our own component is emitting this custom event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.44,
          "end": 287.6,
          "en": "And what do you do with that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 287.6,
          "end": 290.17,
          "en": "Well, you listen to it just as you can listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 290.17,
          "end": 291.84000000000003,
          "en": "to clicks on buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.84000000000003,
          "end": 295.93,
          "en": "In the app.vue file, where we use our own component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 295.93,
          "end": 300.8,
          "en": "you can listen to it with v-on or the @ shorthand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 300.8,
          "end": 304.577,
          "en": "And here we can listen to toggle-favorite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.577,
          "end": 308.877,
          "en": "and bind this to any JavaScript code that should execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 308.877,
          "end": 311.203,
          "en": "when this event is emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 313.3,
          "end": 315.217,
          "en": "Here, we could now add methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 315.217,
          "end": 318.19,
          "en": "to our Vue app config object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 318.19,
          "end": 323.19,
          "en": "and add a method named toggleFavoriteStatus, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.49,
          "end": 330.49,
          "en": "And then bind this method here to our toggle-favorite event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 332.44,
          "end": 335.39,
          "en": "And if we save that, that should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 335.39,
          "end": 337.5,
          "en": "Of course at the moment, that does nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 337.5,
          "end": 340.13,
          "en": "but we also don't get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 340.13,
          "end": 342.04,
          "en": "And we can tell that it works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 342.04,
          "end": 344.75,
          "en": "if we add an alert here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 344.75,
          "end": 347.56,
          "en": "in that toggle favorite status method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 347.56,
          "end": 352.11,
          "en": "This works, which of course is not the final code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 352.11,
          "end": 353.233,
          "en": "but a good test.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 354.38,
          "end": 357.89300000000003,
          "en": "Now you'll see, I get this alert if I click toggle favorite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 358.83,
          "end": 361.14,
          "en": "And that is how we can communicate back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 361.14,
          "end": 363.545,
          "en": "from a component to its parent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 363.545,
          "end": 365.283,
          "en": "But of course we're not done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 366.19,
          "end": 368.54,
          "en": "We're now emitting a custom event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 368.54,
          "end": 372.15,
          "en": "but this event should probably carry some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 372.15,
          "end": 375.85,
          "en": "so that we also let the parent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 375.85,
          "end": 380.42,
          "en": "the app.vue file know which of the two contacts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 380.42,
          "end": 382.74,
          "en": "changed its favorite status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 382.74,
          "end": 387.253,
          "en": "Because we got two and here we got no easy way of telling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 388.25,
          "end": 391.148,
          "en": "Well, in FriendContact.vue, when we emit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 391.148,
          "end": 393.98,
          "en": "we can also pass a second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 393.98,
          "end": 397.15999999999997,
          "en": "Actually, you can pass as many arguments as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 397.15999999999997,
          "end": 401.17,
          "en": "And every extra argument will simply be data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 401.17,
          "end": 403.673,
          "en": "that you pass together with your event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 404.9,
          "end": 406.82,
          "en": "So for example here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 406.82,
          "end": 410.266,
          "en": "we could expect that we get one extra prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 410.266,
          "end": 412.40999999999997,
          "en": "the ID of the friend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 412.40999999999997,
          "end": 416.463,
          "en": "which is of type string and which should be required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 417.8,
          "end": 420.853,
          "en": "So I'm adding this extra prop definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 421.86,
          "end": 426.86,
          "en": "In app.vue, we do have IDs so we can easily pass them in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 427.56,
          "end": 431.48,
          "en": "simply by binding the newly defined ID prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 431.48,
          "end": 434.223,
          "en": "and passing in friends.id like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 435.76,
          "end": 439.07,
          "en": "And now with the ID provided to FriendContact",
          "zh": ""
